Package: scoth.fast
Type: Package
Title: Changepoint Detection via Subset Chains, with a Fast Exact O(T log T) Scoring Algorithm
Version: 1.0.5
Author: Alexis Huet (original scoth package); fast scoring improvement (improvement 5) for a data-mining course project
Maintainer: Alexis Huet <alexis.huet@huawei.com>
Description: Implementation of the chain of subsets change point detection methodology presented in the PAKDD'25 paper.
    [IMPROVEMENT-5] This copy adds an exact fast implementation of the scoring step (Algorithm 1):
    the cuts are kept in a doubly-linked list, the scores in a binary min-heap (ties broken by the
    smallest index, like which.min), and segment costs come from bit-identical replicas of the original
    cost functions (short segments) or O(1) compensated prefix sums (long segments). On the 42 TCPD
    datasets the scores agree with the original ones up to the last bits (bit-identical with
    options(scoth.fast_exact_max_len = Inf)) and all the selections are identical, but the time grows
    as O(T log T) instead of O(T^2). Select it with options(scoth.scoring_algorithm = "fast"); the default ("original") runs the
    reference implementation. The selection step (Algorithm 2) can also use the exact cost replicas with
    options(scoth.fast_selection = TRUE).
